      "description": "Watch Real Sociedad vs Celta Vigo highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 3, 2026. Step into the atmosphere of La Liga as Real Sociedad and Celta Vigo clashed in a match defined by tactical rigidity and defensive resilience. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish dominance in a fixture that promised a high-level strategic battle. Cautious Beginnings at the Anoeta On September 3, 2026 , the Anoeta stadium played host to a contest where chances were at a premium but intensity was high. Real Sociedad looked to exploit set-piece situations early on, with Sergio Gómez delivering a series of corners that tested the visitors' organization. The closest the home side came to an opener was in the 13th minute when Jon Martín connected with a header, only to be denied by a sharp save from Ionut Andrei Radu . Celta Vigo remained disciplined, occasionally threatening from distance through Ilaix Moriba , though his efforts failed to trouble the target. The physical nature of the game saw Yangel Herrera go into the referee's book early for a rough challenge. A defensive lapse by Igor Zubeldia briefly gave the home fans a scare, but the deadlock remained unbroken as both teams headed into the tunnels at halftime. Defensive Heroics and Late Pressure The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to find a breakthrough. Mikel Oyarzabal missed a chance from a direct free kick before the introduction of Iago Aspas for Celta and Gonçalo Guedes for Real Sociedad injected fresh energy into the final third. The match grew increasingly fractious, with Marcos Alonso , Couhaib Driouech , and Luka Sucic all receiving yellow cards as the battle for midfield supremacy intensified. As the clock ticked towards the 90th minute, Gonçalo Guedes nearly snatched victory for the hosts with a powerful strike from outside the box that whistled just wide of the post. Despite a late counter-attack led by Aspas and several desperate crosses from Real Sociedad , the match ended in a goalless draw. Ionut Andrei Radu was arguably the standout performer, commanding his area and ensuring a clean sheet in front of a 30,364-strong crowd."
